file so future containers can be stamped out natively without the shell scripts.\n\n---\n\n**Please confirm if you would like me to proceed with Step 1 (backup) and Step 2 (partitioning the ext4 partition for Cozo).**","thinking":"Container correctness is the priority; the user wants to ensure the base configuration is sound. The user proposes moving from ad-hoc provisioning scripts to a reusable Incus template once the container is finalized. The importance of outlining any potentially irreversible actions before execution is reiterated.\n\n\nFirst, a full backup of the existing image is essential before making any changes to prevent data loss. The user's goal is to create a storage layout with a Btrfs partition for read/write access and an ext4 partition for Cozo database performance. Finally, a separate partition is planned for upgrades, likely employing an overlay to the root filesystem.\n\n\n"}
